{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 65,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician, A Psalm ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Song of David. Praise waiteth for thee, O God, in Zion: and to thee shall the vow be performed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O thou that hearest prayer, to thee shall all flesh come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Iniquities prevail against me: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " our transgressions, thou shalt purge them away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is the man whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou choosest, and causest to approach ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he may dwell in thy courts: we shall be satisfied with the goodness of thy house, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of thy holy temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " terrible things in righteousness wilt thou answer us, O God of our salvation; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "who art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the confidence of all the ends of the earth, and of them that are afar off ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the sea:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who by his strength setteth fast the mountains; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " girded with power:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who stilleth the noise of the seas, the noise of their waves, and the tumult of the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They also that dwell in the uttermost parts are afraid at thy tokens: thou makest the outgoings of the morning and evening to rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou visitest the earth, and waterest it: thou greatly enrichest it with the river of God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is full of water: thou preparest them corn, when thou hast so provided for it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou waterest the ridges of it abundantly: thou settlest the furrows of it: thou makest it soft with showers: thou blessest the springing of it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou crownest the year with thy goodness; and thy paths drop fatness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They drop ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the pastures of the wilderness: and the little hills rejoice on every side.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.65.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.65.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The pastures are clothed with flocks; the valleys also are covered over with corn; they shout for joy, they also sing.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
